## Proposal

### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.
On web, dragging to select report text can throw an uncaught `IndexSizeError: Failed to execute 'setStart' on 'Range': There is no child at offset 13.` during pointer interaction on `SearchMoneyRequestReport`.

### What is the root cause of that problem?
In `src/libs/rescueStuckReportTextSelection/index.ts`, `getCaretRange()` creates a `Range` and calls `range.setStart(position.offsetNode, position.offset)` directly on the raw `CaretPosition` returned by `document.caretPositionFromPoint(x, y)` before any node or offset validation occurs:
https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/5e154c8997c28b79ac0f54a1f58a94c2f229a047/src/libs/rescueStuckReportTextSelection/index.ts#L27-L42

Per the CSSOM View spec, `caretPositionFromPoint()` can return a non-`Text` node — notably an `<input>` or `<textarea>` `Element` as `offsetNode` with `offset` set to the character offset inside its value (e.g. `13`), or another element node. Because `Range.setStart()` interprets `offset` on an `Element` as a child node index rather than a character index, passing an offset greater than `offsetNode.childNodes.length` throws `IndexSizeError`.

`getReportTextPoint()` only checks `isTextNode(node)` after `getCaretRange()` has already thrown:
https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/5e154c8997c28b79ac0f54a1f58a94c2f229a047/src/libs/rescueStuckReportTextSelection/index.ts#L44-L60

Because `getReportTextPoint()` is called from both `onMouseDown()` and `onMouseMove()` outside the `try/catch` around `selection.setBaseAndExtent()`, the error escapes uncaught:
https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/5e154c8997c28b79ac0f54a1f58a94c2f229a047/src/libs/rescueStuckReportTextSelection/index.ts#L86-L98

### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?
`getCaretRange()` is module-private, only used by `getReportTextPoint()`, and the constructed `Range` is immediately discarded after reading `startContainer` and `startOffset`. Instead of creating a `Range`, validate `CaretPosition` directly in `getReportTextPoint()`:

1. Update `CaretPositionFromPoint` in `src/libs/rescueStuckReportTextSelection/index.ts` so `offsetNode` is typed as `Node | null`.
2. Remove `getCaretRange()` and read `document.caretPositionFromPoint` directly inside `getReportTextPoint()`, validating before returning `{node, offset}`:
   - Return `null` if `caretPositionFromPoint` is unavailable or returns `null`.
   - Verify `isTextNode(offsetNode)` and `document.contains(offsetNode)`.
   - Verify `(offsetNode.textContent ?? '').trim()` is non-empty.
   - Verify `Number.isInteger(offset) && offset >= 0 && offset <= text.length`.
   - Verify `offsetNode.parentElement?.closest(REPORT_ACTIONS_LIST_SELECTOR)` matches.

```ts
type CaretPositionFromPoint = (x: number, y: number) => {offsetNode: Node | null; offset: number} | null;

function getReportTextPoint(x: number, y: number): TextPoint | null {
    const caretPositionFromPoint = (document as Document & {caretPositionFromPoint?: CaretPositionFromPoint}).caretPositionFromPoint;
    if (typeof caretPositionFromPoint !== 'function') {
        return null;
    }

    const position = caretPositionFromPoint.call(document, x, y);
    if (!position) {
        return null;
    }

    const {offsetNode, offset} = position;
    if (!isTextNode(offsetNode) || !document.contains(offsetNode)) {
        return null;
    }

    const text = offsetNode.textContent ?? '';
    if (!text.trim()) {
        return null;
    }

    if (!Number.isInteger(offset) || offset < 0 || offset > text.length) {
        return null;
    }

    if (!offsetNode.parentElement?.closest(REPORT_ACTIONS_LIST_SELECTOR)) {
        return null;
    }

    return {node: offsetNode, offset};
}
```

### What specific scenarios should we cover in automated tests?
Add unit tests in `tests/unit/RescueStuckReportTextSelectionTest.ts` covering:
- `caretPositionFromPoint` returning a non-text element (`<input>` / `<textarea>` / `<div>`) with an offset larger than its child count (e.g. `13`) during both `mousedown` and `mousemove` — does not throw and leaves selection unchanged.
- `caretPositionFromPoint` returning `null`, a detached `Text` node, a whitespace-only `Text` node, a `Text` node outside `REPORT_ACTIONS_LIST_SELECTOR`, or a `Text` node with an out-of-bounds/negative offset (`-1`, `text.length + 1`, `NaN`) — safely ignored without throwing.
- Valid report `Text` nodes inside `REPORT_ACTIONS_LIST` and `MONEY_REQUEST_REPORT_ACTIONS_LIST` still rescue a stuck drag selection via `selection.setBaseAndExtent()`.

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)
Keeping `getCaretRange()` and validating `offsetNode`/`offset` (or wrapping `range.setStart()` in `try/catch`) before creating the `Range`. Since `Range` is never used anywhere else in this module, validating and returning the `TextPoint` directly is simpler, avoids unnecessary DOM `Range` allocations on every `mousemove`, and eliminates the `Range.setStart()` failure mode completely.

